pretty simple challenge 

we are given a file, and told to find the flag 

at first i wanted to know what type of file it is so i ran files cmd and just printed data 

and using exiftool it said unknown file type 

so i used ghex and found that the header was corrupted and it it started with 89 and 50 this gave me the clue that it was a PNG file format 

so i opened the file in hexeditor 

using hexeditor -n 

and then i replaced the corrupted bits with the proper PNG header which i got from the wiki 

then saved the new fixed file as .png file and opened it 

it was a black red image at first glance 

then i used an online tool https://29a.ch/photo-forensics/#forensic-magnifier

and saw that the flag was hidden inside 

there is another way to find the flag 

using python cv we can solve this and add an mask to find the flag 

the reference writeup is 

